---
// src/pages/en/portfolio/qa-agent-supervisor.astro
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="QA Agent Supervisor | Multi-agent orchestrator for Playwright tests"
  description="Multi-agent system (LangGraph + Claude API + Pydantic) that orchestrates and analyzes a real Playwright/pytest test suite: coverage suggestions, failure triage, reliable flaky test detection, two-tier reports."
  lang="en"
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="project-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-back">
        <a href="/en/portfolio" class="back-link">← Back to portfolio</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="hero-badge">AI agents applied to testing</div>
        <h1>QA Agent Supervisor</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">
          A multi-agent system that runs a real Playwright/pytest test suite
          for an e-commerce site. It suggests coverage ideas, runs the tests,
          triages failures and writes the report, without ever writing test
          code itself.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/berangeregallais/qa-agent-supervisor"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            View the code on GitHub →
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-image">
          <img
            src="/portfolio/qa-agent-supervisor-report.png"
            alt="Report generated by QA Agent Supervisor: run history, pass rate and summary"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section class="overview-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Overview</h2>
      <div class="overview-grid">
        <div class="overview-card">
          <div class="overview-icon">🎯</div>
          <h3>The problem</h3>
          <p>
            A Playwright/pytest test suite produces failures, but someone
            has to triage them: product bug, brittle test, flaky, or
            environment issue. Having an AI generate test code on the fly
            was tried, then abandoned: the result was too unstable to trust.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="overview-card">
          <div class="overview-icon">🧭</div>
          <h3>The approach</h3>
          <p>
            A Supervisor agent routes each request to one of 4 specialized
            agents via LangGraph. Each agent has a single responsibility and
            a typed output (Pydantic), guaranteed by Claude Structured
            Outputs rather than free-text parsing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="overview-card">
          <div class="overview-icon">🔍</div>
          <h3>The rigor</h3>
          <p>
            A test is only labeled flaky if it fails then passes in the same
            run (via pytest-rerunfailures), never by a guess based on its
            history. Only failures that persist after that rerun trigger a
            call to Claude.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Technical Architecture -->
  <section class="architecture-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Architecture</h2>

      <div class="architecture-overview">
        <h3>Supervisor pattern (LangGraph)</h3>
        <p>
          A central node (the Supervisor) receives each request and routes it
          to one of 4 specialized agents based on its type. Every agent
          communicates through structured Pydantic outputs, guaranteed by
          Claude Structured Outputs: no agent parses free text produced by
          another.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Architecture diagram -->
      <div class="architecture-diagram">
        <div class="mermaid">
          graph TD;
            start([User request]):::first
            supervisor(Supervisor)
            analyst(Analyst)
            executor(Executor)
            triage(Triage)
            reporter(Reporter)
            done([Response]):::last
            start --> supervisor;
            supervisor --> analyst;
            supervisor --> executor;
            supervisor --> triage;
            supervisor --> reporter;
            analyst --> supervisor;
            executor --> supervisor;
            triage --> supervisor;
            reporter --> done;
            classDef default fill:#f2f0ff,line-height:1.2
            classDef first fill-opacity:0
            classDef last fill:#bfb6fc
        </div>
        <p class="diagram-caption">
          The Supervisor routes each request to the appropriate specialized
          agent
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-grid">
        <div class="architecture-card">
          <div class="node-number">1</div>
          <h4>Analyst</h4>
          <p>
            Suggests untested coverage ideas from a natural-language spec,
            checking the actual list of existing tests so it never suggests
            duplicate coverage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-card">
          <div class="node-number">2</div>
          <h4>Executor</h4>
          <p>
            Runs the real pytest suite as a subprocess and parses the
            resulting JUnit XML, including the full error text, not just a
            truncated summary.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-card">
          <div class="node-number">3</div>
          <h4>Triage</h4>
          <p>
            Categorizes each failure: product bug, brittle test, flaky, or
            environment issue. Tests that pass after a rerun are classified
            "flaky" by direct evidence, with no LLM call; only persistent
            failures go through Claude.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-card">
          <div class="node-number">4</div>
          <h4>Reporter</h4>
          <p>
            Produces a two-tier report: a full technical report for dev/QA
            teams, and a jargon-free, 3-sentence summary for non-technical
            readers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Interface -->
  <section class="interface-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Web interface</h2>
      <div class="interface-content">
        <ul class="interface-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Test selection</strong> and asynchronous run launching
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Stop button</strong> that actually kills the running pytest
            subprocess (verified live: ~45 ms response time)
          </li>
          <li><strong>Run history</strong> and CSV/JSON export</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cost estimate</strong> before launching a run
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="interface-image">
        <img
          src="/portfolio/qa-agent-supervisor-report.png"
          alt="Full report generated by QA Agent Supervisor after a run"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tech Stack -->
  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Tech Stack</h2>

      <div class="stack-grid">
        <div class="stack-category">
          <h3>Agents & AI</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Python 3.13</strong> - Main language</li>
            <li>
              <strong>LangGraph 1.2.11</strong> - Multi-agent orchestration (Supervisor
              pattern)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Claude API (claude-opus-5)</strong> - via <code
                >messages.parse()</code
              > with typed output
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Prompt caching</strong> - <code
                >cache_control: ephemeral</code
              > on system prompts
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Pydantic 2.13</strong> - Typed data contract between agents
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="stack-category">
          <h3>Backend & Interface</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>FastAPI + Uvicorn</strong> - API</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Vanilla JavaScript / HTML</strong> - Frontend, no framework
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="stack-category">
          <h3>Tests under orchestration</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>pytest + pytest-rerunfailures</strong> - Real Playwright suite
              (separate project)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>JUnit XML</strong> - Test result exchange format
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="stack-category">
          <h3>Quality & CI</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>81 automated tests</strong> on the agents themselves, 100%
              mocked
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>GitHub Actions</strong> - CI with no secret required
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Metrics -->
  <section class="metrics-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Real metrics</h2>

      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <div class="metric-card">
          <div class="metric-value">81</div>
          <div class="metric-label">
            Automated tests on the agents, 100% mocked (no real Claude calls
            or pytest subprocess)
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-card">
          <div class="metric-value">~45ms</div>
          <div class="metric-label">
            Run cancellation response time (verified live)
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-card">
          <div class="metric-value">4-8</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Claude calls per real run</div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-card">
          <div class="metric-value">$0.04–0.24</div>
          <div class="metric-label">
            Estimated cost per run, depending on whether suggestions/triage
            are triggered
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="metrics-note">
        I don't have a metric like "% more bugs caught": that would need to
        be measured over real usage over time. I'd rather not quote a number
        I haven't verified.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Section -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-content">
        <h2>Questions about the architecture?</h2>
        <p>
          The full code, including architecture decisions and abandoned
          approaches, is documented in the repo's README.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-buttons">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/berangeregallais/qa-agent-supervisor"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="btn btn-primary btn-large"
          >
            View the GitHub repo
          </a>
          <a href="/en/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Variables */
  :root {
    --section-spacing: 4rem;
  }

  /* Hero Section */
  .project-hero {
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgb(var(--color-background)) 0%,
      rgba(var(--color-primary), 0.05) 100%
    );
  }

  .hero-back {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: rgb(var(--color-primary));
  }

  .hero-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgb(var(--color-accent)),
      rgba(var(--color-accent), 0.75)
    );
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-button));
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .project-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-image {
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl);
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
    height: 520px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .hero-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top;
  }

  .hero-image::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent,
      rgba(var(--color-background), 0.95)
    );
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Overview Section */
  .overview-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
    background: rgb(var(--color-surface));
  }

  .overview-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .overview-card {
    background: rgba(var(--color-surface-variant), 0.3);
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .overview-icon {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .overview-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .overview-card p {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Architecture Section */
  .architecture-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
    background: rgba(var(--color-surface-variant), 0.3);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }

  .architecture-overview {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
  }

  .architecture-overview h3 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .architecture-overview p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .architecture-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .architecture-card {
    background: rgb(var(--color-surface));
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .node-number {
    position: absolute;
    top: -15px;
    left: 20px;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgb(var(--color-primary)),
      rgb(var(--color-primary-hover))
    );
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-button));
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .architecture-card h4 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .architecture-card p {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* Architecture Diagram */
  .architecture-diagram {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    text-align: center;
    background: rgba(var(--color-primary), 0.02);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.1);
  }

  .mermaid {
    background: white;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .diagram-caption {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Interface Section */
  .interface-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
  }

  .interface-content {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .interface-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .interface-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .interface-list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: rgb(var(--color-success));
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .interface-list strong {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }

  .interface-image {
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    max-width: 900px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl);
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
  }

  .interface-image img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Stack Section */
  .stack-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
    background: rgba(var(--color-surface-variant), 0.3);
  }

  .stack-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .stack-category {
    background: rgb(var(--color-surface));
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .stack-category h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-primary));
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(var(--color-primary), 0.3);
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .stack-category ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .stack-category ul li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.2);
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .stack-category ul li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .stack-category strong {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }

  /* Metrics Section */
  .metrics-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgba(var(--color-primary), 0.05) 0%,
      rgba(var(--color-accent), 0.03) 100%
    );
  }

  .metrics-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .metric-card {
    background: rgb(var(--color-surface));
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-border), 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .metric-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl);
  }

  .metric-value {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgb(var(--color-primary));
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .metric-label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
  }

  .metrics-note {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* CTA Section */
  .cta-section {
    padding: var(--section-spacing) 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .cta-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cta-content p {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .overview-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .stack-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .metrics-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    :root {
      --section-spacing: 2.5rem;
    }

    .project-hero {
      padding: 3rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .hero-image {
      height: 320px;
    }

    .architecture-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .metrics-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cta-buttons {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }
</style>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@10.6.1/dist/mermaid.min.js"></script>
<script>
  declare const mermaid: any;
  mermaid.initialize({
    startOnLoad: true,
    theme: 'default',
    flowchart: {
      curve: 'linear'
    }
  });
</script>
